  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all incidents reported within 24 hours, customer notice within 24 hours, no phase-in. S2 keeps a 5% limit but gives existing models a 36-month transition with no interim cap, and results go to customers/regulators but not the public, which favors Northwind. S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with no transition, severely hurting Halcyon given Ember 8's 9.9 rate; S4's 36-month suppression deadline meets Halcyon's red line, but overall the deal favors Northwind."
